# No d3d9 flag: Gallium Nine is gone from mesa. media-libs/mesa-26.0.8 has no
# `d3d9` and no `nine` anywhere in the ebuild, so the flag named a state mesa can
# no longer be in -- and Portage ignores an unknown package.use flag in silence
# (checked 2026-09-08).
media-libs/mesa lm-sensors opencl
media-libs/libvpx postproc
# libdrm[video_cards_radeon] is REQUIRED, and the reason is not mesa.
#
# It was removed on 2026-09-09 on the grounds that no consumer wanted it -- that
# search covered media-libs/mesa and x11-drivers/*, and missed x11-base/. The
# real chain is:
#     VIDEO_CARDS=radeonsi -> x11-base/xorg-drivers
#                          -> x11-drivers/xf86-video-ati
#                          -> >=x11-libs/libdrm-2.4.89[video_cards_radeon]
# xf86-video-ati serves BOTH radeon and radeonsi, and its libdrm dependency is
# unconditional. step12-kde-resolve stopped on exactly this, asking for the flag
# back (lab, 2026-09-12).
x11-libs/libdrm video_cards_radeon
media-libs/vulkan-loader layers
